    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18617" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχαία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχαιΐη</span></b> , ἡ, epith. of Demeter in Attica, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			5.61
		</span></i>; also in Boeotia, <i><span class="en">
			Plu.
			2.378e
		</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχέα</span> at Thespiae, <i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			7.1867
		</span></i>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀχαιά</span></b> , ἡ, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔριθος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Philet.
			</span></i> ap. Gramm. post Orionem <i><span class="en">
				p.185S.
			</span></i> (Acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄχος</span>
			<i>grief</i> for the loss of her daughter: also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχηρώ</span></b>  Id.) <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχαΐα</span></b> , 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχαιός.</span>
			</div>
